{"slug":"emanuel-cleaver","qid":"Q1334654","name":"Emanuel Cleaver","desc":"U.S. Representative from Missouri","article":"Emanuel Cleaver","born":"1944-10-26","died":null,"birthplace":"Waxahachie","parties":["Democratic Party"],"offices":[{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"MO-05","f":2005,"u":null},{"t":"Mayor of Kansas City, Missouri","w":"","f":1991,"u":1999},{"t":"Mayor of Kansas City","w":"","f":1991,"u":1999}],"summary":"Emanuel Cleaver II (born October 26, 1944) is an American politician and United Methodist pastor serving as the U.S. representative for Missouri's 5th congressional district since 2005. A member of the Democratic Party, he previously served as the 51st mayor of Kansas City, Missouri, from 1991 to 1999, becoming the first Black person to hold that role.\nCleaver represents a district that primarily consists of the inner ring of the Kansas City metropolitan area, including nearly all of Kansas City and some of its suburbs in Clay and Jackson counties, including North Kansas City, Gladstone, Independence, Lee's Summit, and some of Blue Springs.","photo":{"f":"emanuel-cleaver.jpg","by":"US House Office of Photography","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":null,"page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emanuel_Cleaver_official_photo.jpg"},"history":[{"y":2026,"o":"H","k":"MO-05","p":"D","n":"Emanuel Cleaver","race":"MO-05"},{"y":2024,"o":"H","k":"MO-05","p":"D","v":199900,"s":60.22,"w":true,"n":"Emanuel Cleaver"},{"y":2022,"o":"H","k":"MO-05","p":"D","v":140688,"s":61.02,"w":true,"n":"Emanuel Cleaver"},{"y":2020,"o":"H","k":"MO-05","p":"D","v":207180,"s":58.79,"w":true,"n":"Emanuel Cleaver"},{"y":2018,"o":"H","k":"MO-05","p":"D","v":175019,"s":61.67,"w":true,"n":"Emanuel Cleaver II"},{"y":2016,"o":"H","k":"MO-05","p":"D","v":190766,"s":58.83,"w":true,"n":"Emanuel Cleaver"},{"y":2014,"o":"H","k":"MO-05","p":"D","v":79256,"s":51.59,"w":true,"n":"Emanuel Cleaver"},{"y":2012,"o":"H","k":"MO-05","p":"D","v":200290,"s":60.52,"w":true,"n":"Emanuel Cleaver"},{"